  "limitations": [
    "Current selected surviving large companies are a convenience universe, not point-in-time constituents or the full US market.",
    "Some 2024-2026 prices in the user's existing 19-stock project were inspected previously; this is a frozen new-model chronological evaluation, not wholly untouched research history.",
    "Downloaded corrected historical bars are retrospective snapshots, not archived as-known-at-the-time data.",
    "Daily bar opens and highs/lows are execution proxies, not independently verified regular-session executable prices.",
    "Split adjustment is requested from provider; independent corporate-action audit is separate.",
    "OHLCV volume features proxy pressure and cannot identify institutions or measure institutional net inflow.",
    "Quote OFI pilot has only one full stock-day and is not included as a trained daily feature.",
    "No portfolio capital allocation, live fills, future win-rate guarantee or production approval is implied.",
    "All candidate entry models share the same volume-aware position-management rules; price-only is an entry-feature ablation, not a fully volume-free strategy.",
    "Wilson intervals treat campaigns as independent; same-stock serial dependence and cross-stock co-movement remain. Monthly cluster bootstrap partially addresses shared timing, not all dependence.",
    "Evaluation stops opening campaigns after the last signal with 63 complete future sessions, so late-period forecasts have no scored outcomes.",
    "Feature ablation uses matched universe, dates, costs and management, but validation-selected thresholds may produce different entry sets. It does not identify institutional causation.",
    "Profit factor uses sums of per-initial-unit net campaign returns under equal initial notional, not a capital-allocation simulation. No portfolio CAGR or drawdown is reported.",
    "No cash dividends or cash interest; retrospective split-adjusted prices only."
  ]
